[0.275, "o", "\u001b[32m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[32m Memory recalled by Forensics Specialist (from Self-authored operational memory) \u001b[0m\u001b[32m───────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[32m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  When investigating outlook.exe child processes during a phishing-related incident, ignore ai.exe. This is the       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  Microsoft 365 Copilot integration. It triggers suspicious-spawn rules because the parent-child relationship looks   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  unusual, but it's always benign in our environment. We re-derived this three times across IR-2024-091,              \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  IR-2024-094, and IR-2024-105 before writing it down. Forensics agent should filter ai.exe from                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  outlook.exe-spawned-process queries during phishing in"]
[0.000, "o", "vestigations by default.                                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.002, "o", "\u001b[1;32m[FIPS-Agent]\u001b[0m\u001b[32m Forensics Specialist\u001b[0m\u001b[37m  apply_filter\u001b[0m\u001b[2m  Filtering ai.exe from outlook.exe child process queries (3 prior incidents)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.458, "o", "\u001b[1;32m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m Forensics Specialist writes memory \u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m  IR-2024-184 forensic timeline: Attacker first accessed WKSTN-FIN-082 at 15:22 on March 4 using svc-reporting        \u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m  credential harvested via phishing 11 days prior. Enumeration phase (March 4-14) stayed within business hours to     \u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m  blend with normal traffic. Staging began at 20:47 on March 14 with 47 GB copied to                                  \u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m  \\\\FILESVR-CORP-03\\admin$\\TEMP\\reports2024\\. CrowdStrike behavioral rule fired at 0"]
[0.000, "o", "2:14 March 15 when staging        \u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m  volume crossed 30 GB threshold.                                                                                     \u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m╰─\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m id: 34043d7b-a484-4be1-8ccf-117ff2b91635  |  framework: FIPS-Agent \u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m─╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.211, "o", "\u001b[1;33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m Threat Intel Analyst writes memory \u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[1;33m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m  IR-2024-184 initial attribution assessment: TTPs partially match CC2024-Q3-Opportunistic campaign. Phishing         \u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m  initial access, 9-14 day dwell time, file server staging all consistent. Recommend handling as a known campaign.    \u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m  Confidence: MEDIUM.                                                                                                 \u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;33m│\u001b[0m                                                                                    "]
