[0.282, "o", "\u001b[35m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[35m Memory recalled by Incident Commander (from IR-2024-103 operational lesson) \u001b[0m\u001b[35m───────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[35m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m│\u001b[0m  Last time we rotated the breakglass credential during an active incident (IR-2024-103), the rotation broke our      \u001b[35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m│\u001b[0m  Veeam backup service for 6 hours because the backup service uses the breakglass credential for restore operations   \u001b[35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m│\u001b[0m  and we hadn't documented that dependency. We had a separate near-miss when network monitoring alerted but ops       \u001b[35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m│\u001b[0m  didn't know it was related to our incident response. Operational lesson: coordinate breakglass rotation with        \u001b[35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m│\u001b[0m  backup admin BEFORE execution, and notify NOC "]
