[2.721, "o", "\u001b[1;35m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m Incident Commander writes memory \u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m  IR-2024-184 confirms the IR-2024-117 attacker pattern is still active. Two things we learned: (1) the attacker      \u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m  waited 11 days between credential harvest and first lateral movement, longer than the 9 days in IR-2024-117. Our    \u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m  default 'go back 14 days' assumption needs to extend to 21 days. (2) The attacker used normal working hours during  \u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m  enumeration, then switched to off-hours during staging. Hunting hypothesis: wh"]
[0.000, "o", "en investigating service account      \u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m  anomalies, also pull the human user's recent access patterns and look for time-of-day shifts.                       \u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;35m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;35m╰─\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m──────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m id: 23e32d03-f731-4b1a-b046-18016c86c0a3  |  framework: OpenClaw \u001b[0m\u001b[1;35m─╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.162, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[1;34m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m───────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m MEMORYHUB: THE CONTEXT THAT MAKES SECURITY DECISIONS GO WELL \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m───────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[1;37mWhat you just saw:\u001b[0m                                                                                                \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m    1. Tier 1 escalated at 02:38 because the agent fleet remembered IR-2024-117 \u001b[36m(Claude Code)\u001b[0m                         \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m    2. Forensics filtered ai.exe false positives from self-authored operational memory \u001b[32m(FIPS-Agent)\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[0m                   \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m    3. Threat Intel's attribution was contradicted and the investigation adjusted \u001b[33m(Hermes)\u001b[0m                            \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m    4. Breakglass rotation didn't break backup because an 8-month-old lesson surfaced \u001b[35m(OpenClaw)\u001b[0m                      \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m    5. Audit trail answers both 'what did this role do?' and 'what was done on behalf of this analyst?'               \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m    \u001b[1mFour frameworks. One shared memory. Zero integration code beyond pointing each agent at the same MCP server.\u001b[0m      \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                      \u001b[1;34m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;34m╰────────────────────"]
